gate: CLOSED
v:4 c:$ m:navitrack-config role:dev x:architect
task: S19 T9 — Sensor profile template, one live product
sprint: S19
dep: S19-T8-about-screen-pass.pd
requires: [ARCHITECT, FRONTEND_DEV, BUN]
test_mandate: ../intel/TEST-COVERAGE-MANDATE.md
quality_mandate: ../intel/CODE-QUALITY-MANDATE.md
invariants: ../S19-INVARIANTS.md

context: |
  Catalog is already a data list: one live fuel BLE product, two comingSoon.
  Session screens are hardcoded to that fuel DUT, not to a profile.
  Add a profile the catalog entry points at (id, transport, which session
  sections exist). The live fuel profile enables today's sections.
  A comingSoon entry must not open a session. Do not add a second live
  sensor, RS-485, or new protocol commands. Prove a fixture profile can
  omit a section without copying SensorSessionScreen.
  Package manager: bun.

out:
  - sensor profile module + catalog link
  - session reads the active profile
  - co-located tests
  - note in S19-INVARIANTS.md

cmd:
  - bun run test

done:
  - Live fuel profile still opens the current session
  - Disabled / comingSoon profile does not
  - Section list comes from the profile
  - `bun run test` passes
